hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2716","I read to Ahmad ibn Abi Shurayh al-Razi that Umar ibn Mujammi' al-Kindi informed them on the authority of Musa ibn 'Uqba, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had his mount stood upright at the Masjid of Dhul-Hulaifa during a Hajj or 'Umrah"","" he would declare the Talbiyah"","" saying: 'Labbayk Allahumma Labbayk"","" Labbayk la"""""
